&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Stop generating&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;contain.text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Stopped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;m1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;this must be ignored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}))&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByTestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;assistant-m1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;not.contain.text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;must be ignored&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The reducer or stream consumer should ignore events belonging to an aborted generation. Also test duplicate tool completions, failure after partial text, retry, and unmount while streaming.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Test the failure state without deleting useful evidence
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A transport can fail after several tokens have rendered. Unless the product intentionally discards them, the partial answer should remain visible and be marked incomplete:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;then&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;m1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Partial answer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;messageId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;m1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Connection lost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByTestId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;assistant-m1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;have.text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Partial answer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;alert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;contain.text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Connection lost&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;findByRole&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Retry&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;should&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;be.enabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Use accessible roles for status, alert, progress, and controls so the test protects keyboard and screen-reader behavior as well as component state. A streaming interface that visually updates but never announces completion is still broken for part of its audience.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Do not overuse &lt;code&gt;cy.clock()&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;cy.clock()&lt;/code&gt; is useful for retry countdowns, debounce, or a delayed “still working” message. It controls timer APIs. It does not automatically control arbitrary Promises, async iterators, or server delivery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Control the stream for causality; control the clock only for behavior that genuinely depends on time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Keep a separate provider contract
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This component test does not prove that the real provider emits your &lt;code&gt;ChatEvent&lt;/code&gt; schema. Keep a smaller integration test for the adapter:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;provider frames parse correctly;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;error frames map to &lt;code&gt;failed&lt;/code&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;abort closes the request;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;secrets and raw prompts are not unintentionally logged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Model-quality evaluation is another suite again. Separating UI behavior, transport compatibility, and semantic quality keeps failures understandable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The useful test matrix is event-oriented: success with tokens, success with a tool, failure before the first token, failure after partial output, user cancellation, duplicate events, and retry. It is much smaller and more reproducible than sampling many model sentences.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Which of your current “LLM test” failures could be reproduced as a five-event fixture instead?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  References
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.cypress.io/app/component-testing/react/examples" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Cypress React Component Testing examples&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.cypress.io/api/commands/clock" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;code&gt;cy.clock()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frontend interviews can be challenging, even when you have hands-on experience with React and JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You might understand how to build a component, manage state, and call APIs, but interviews often test much more: JavaScript fundamentals, problem-solving, React concepts, performance optimization, and your ability to explain technical decisions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The biggest challenge isn't always learning more. It's knowing &lt;strong&gt;what to prepare, in what order, and how to practise consistently.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a practical roadmap you can use to organize your preparation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Week 1: Strengthen Your JavaScript Fundamentals
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JavaScript is one of the most important areas to prepare for a frontend interview.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Focus on:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;var&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;let&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;const&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope, closures, and hoisting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promises, &lt;code&gt;async/await&lt;/code&gt;, and error handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The event loop and microtasks versus macrotasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Array methods such as &lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;filter&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;reduce&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Objects, references, shallow copies, and deep copies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practice challenge:&lt;/strong&gt; Explain the difference between &lt;code&gt;Promise.all()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Promise.allSettled()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Promise.all()&lt;/code&gt; rejects when one of its input promises rejects. &lt;code&gt;Promise.allSettled()&lt;/code&gt; waits until all input promises settle and returns the outcome of each one.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Don't stop at memorizing definitions. Practise explaining when you would use each method in a real application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Week 2: Focus on React and TypeScript
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once your JavaScript fundamentals are solid, move to React.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Important topics include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Props, state, and component rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controlled and uncontrolled components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context API and Redux&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Component composition and reusable hooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React performance optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TypeScript interfaces, types, generics, and utility types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practice challenge:&lt;/strong&gt; When would you use &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; instead of &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; caches a calculated value, while &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; caches a function reference between renders when its dependencies haven't changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In an interview, also explain why neither should be added everywhere automatically. First identify a meaningful performance or reference-stability problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Week 3: Practise Real-World Frontend Engineering
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Interviewers may want to understand how you build and maintain production applications, not just how well you know individual APIs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Prepare for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HTML semantics and CSS layouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsive design and accessibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API integration and loading/error states&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unit testing and component testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Browser rendering and frontend performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server-side rendering and client-side rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microfrontend architecture and module federation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practice challenge:&lt;/strong&gt; How would you improve the performance of a React page that renders slowly?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A structured answer might cover measuring the issue first, identifying unnecessary renders, reducing expensive calculations, splitting large bundles, optimizing network requests, and checking whether large lists need virtualization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The important part is explaining how you would identify the bottleneck before choosing a solution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Week 4: Simulate the Interview
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use the final week to combine what you've learned.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Try to complete:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript coding problems under time limits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A small React machine-coding exercise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A frontend architecture discussion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A review of common technical questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mock interviews where you explain your answers aloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After each session, record the topics you struggled with and revisit them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A Simple Daily Study Routine
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you have around two hours a day, try this schedule:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;30 minutes:&lt;/strong&gt; Review concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;45 minutes:&lt;/strong&gt; Solve coding problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;30 minutes:&lt;/strong&gt; Practise explaining answers aloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;15 minutes:&lt;/strong&gt; Review mistakes and note what to revisit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consistency is more valuable than trying to study everything in a single weekend.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Common Interview Preparation Mistakes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A few mistakes can make preparation less effective:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Memorizing answers without understanding the underlying concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Studying React while neglecting JavaScript fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Watching tutorials without writing code yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ignoring testing, accessibility, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Never practising answers under interview conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A structured plan helps you identify gaps and measure progress.&lt;/p&gt;

