&lt;h2&gt;


  Let's Discuss
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're preparing for a frontend interview, which area do you find most challenging?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript coding questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React concepts and hooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Machine-coding rounds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Share your experience in the comments. Your answer might help another developer prepare more effectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SWAPI (The Star Wars API) is one of the most popular free APIs for learning REST APIs in React, Vue, or vanilla JS — but it only returns JSON text. There are no images for Luke Skywalker, Tatooine, or the Millennium Falcon.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Furthermore, the old image host frequently used in tutorials (starwars-visualguide.com) currently has broken SSL certificates, failing to load across modern browsers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To solve this, I created a free static image API where every image matches the exact same ID used by SWAPI:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/%7Bcategory%7D/%7Bid%7D.jpg" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/{category}/{id}.jpg&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It covers 238 images across 5 categories: people, planets, species, starships, and vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  How to Use It (JavaScript)
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
javascript
const getSwapiImage = (category, swapiUrl) =&amp;gt; {
  const id = swapiUrl.split('/').filter(Boolean).pop();
  return `https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/${category}/${id}.jpg`;
};

// Fetch data from SWAPI
const res = await fetch('https://swapi.dev/api/people/1/');
const luke = await res.json();

// Get the matching image
const imageUrl = getSwapiImage('people', luke.url);
console.log(imageUrl); 
// Output: "https://starwarsgallery.netlify.app/assets/people/1.jpg"
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3tm1g6vyrw1xd0ogs160.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F3tm1g6vyrw1xd0ogs160.png" alt=" " width="800" height="595"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building modern React interfaces is hard enough. Why spend hours rebuilding components, designing UI blocks, and creating AI interfaces from scratch?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Meet &lt;strong&gt;SonoJS&lt;/strong&gt;: a React and Tailwind CSS UI library built to help you ship beautiful, production-ready interfaces faster, including UI for AI-powered applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  🤖 Build AI Interfaces Faster
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SonoJS includes UI components and blocks that help you build modern AI experiences without starting from zero. Spend less time on repetitive UI work and more time building your product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  ✨ What's Inside?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Beautiful UI components&lt;/strong&gt; — reusable, customizable building blocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ready-to-use UI blocks&lt;/strong&gt; — assemble complete interface sections faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;AI-focused components&lt;/strong&gt; — building blocks for modern AI application interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive charts&lt;/strong&gt; — bring data to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Developer tools&lt;/strong&gt; — practical utilities for everyday development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Icon collection&lt;/strong&gt; — icons for developers, crypto, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;RTL and LTR support&lt;/strong&gt; — build for different writing directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dark mode&lt;/strong&gt; — support different visual preferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;MCP support&lt;/strong&gt; — connect AI-assisted workflows with your UI development process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  🧑‍💻 Your Components. Your Code.
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With the SonoJS CLI, components are copied directly into your project. You can inspect, edit, and customize the source code instead of relying on a locked-in component package.&lt;/p&gt;

