&lt;p&gt;We make &lt;a href="https://kerf.site/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Kerf&lt;/a&gt;, a WordPress theme that imports websites made by AI tools. One question comes up again and again: &lt;em&gt;“I built my site with Lovable (or Bolt, or v0). Can I put it on WordPress?”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The honest answer is: not by importing it—not with Kerf, and not with any tool that works from HTML. Here’s why, and what you can do instead.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why a React App Is Different from an HTML Website
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Tools like ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Google Stitch can give you &lt;strong&gt;HTML files&lt;/strong&gt;: open &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; and the whole page is there—every heading, paragraph and picture written out in the file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Lovable, Bolt and v0 typically build &lt;strong&gt;React apps&lt;/strong&gt;. Their source is components and a &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt;; a build step bundles it into JavaScript, and the page is assembled in the visitor’s browser when that JavaScript runs. Open the built &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; and you’ll mostly find an empty container like &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div id="root"&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An HTML importer turns the elements in the HTML into editable blocks. When the elements only exist after a script builds them, there is nothing in the file to turn into blocks. That’s why Kerf doesn’t import these apps yet—and why its pre-import check tells you so before anything changes on your site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Your Real Options
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Keep the App Where It Is, and Add WordPress Next to It
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the site is mostly an app—logins, dashboards, live data—keep hosting it where it runs well today (for example Netlify or Vercel). If you also want a blog or editable marketing pages, run WordPress alongside it, for example on a subdomain, and link between the two.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. Use WordPress as the Content Source (Headless)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A developer can keep the React front end and have it fetch posts and pages from WordPress’s REST API. Editors write in WordPress; the app shows the content. It’s flexible, but it is a development project, not a one-click move, and the WordPress block editor won’t show your app’s design while you edit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Rebuild the Pages in WordPress
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a simple marketing site, rebuilding by hand in a page builder or block theme works. It takes time, and the result is a look-alike rather than the same design.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Recreate the Design as Plain HTML, Then Import It
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If what you love is the &lt;em&gt;look&lt;/em&gt;, not the app logic, you can ask an AI tool to recreate the pages as plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript—no React, no build step. That version is a normal website, and an HTML website can be imported into WordPress as editable blocks. Our &lt;a href="https://kerf.site/blog/claude-chatgpt-gemini-to-wordpress/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;prompt brief for WordPress-ready AI HTML&lt;/a&gt; lists what to ask for.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;


  How to Tell Which Kind You Have
&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If your project has a &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; and you need to run something like &lt;code&gt;npm run build&lt;/code&gt; to see it, it’s an app. If you can double-click &lt;code&gt;index.html&lt;/code&gt; and see the full page with its words in the file, it’s HTML—and that’s the kind Kerf imports.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What Kerf Is For
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Kerf is built for HTML websites: the ZIP you get from ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Google Stitch, or from a designer. It keeps the same tags, classes, stylesheets and scripts, and makes every word, picture and menu editable in WordPress. If that’s what you have, you can &lt;a href="https://kerf.site/demo/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;try it free in your browser&lt;/a&gt;—a private WordPress with Kerf installed, no sign-up.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://kerf.site/blog/lovable-bolt-v0-to-wordpress/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;kerf.site&lt;/a&gt;. Try Kerf free in your browser — a private WordPress with Kerf installed, no sign-up: &lt;a href="https://kerf.site/demo/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://kerf.site/demo/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;​Today, I revised some of the core fundamentals of React JS. Sharing my simple notes here for anyone starting out with React:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​1. SPA (Single Page Application):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
React apps load a single HTML page and dynamically update the content, making the app super fast and smooth! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​2. JSX (JavaScript XML):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
It lets us write HTML and XML-like syntax directly inside JavaScript.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​3. Running the App:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Use the simple command npm run dev to start your development server.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​4. useState Hook:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
​Used to manage state (data) in functional components.&lt;br&gt;
​Syntax: const [variable, function] = useState(initialValue);&lt;br&gt;
​Example: const [count, setCount] = useState(0);&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​5. rfce Shortcut:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
A handy shortcut in VS Code to quickly generate a React Functional Component Skeleton! &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I build &lt;a href="https://qrflows.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;QRflows&lt;/a&gt;, a dynamic QR code platform. Last week I was going through session recordings and found our most engaged user of the month: someone in Hong Kong who spent 11 minutes in the dashboard, clicked 82 times, tried half a dozen QR types, added a logo, built a landing page.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At minute three, the page crashed and reloaded.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The error in the console:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;NotFoundError: Failed to execute 'removeChild' on 'Node':
The node to be removed is not a child of this node.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The recording made the cause obvious once I noticed it: the whole dashboard was in Chinese. Our site only exists in English. The user had Chrome's built-in Google Translate turned on.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is one of those bugs that never shows up in your own testing, because you never translate your own app. Here's what's going on, how to reproduce it without Google Translate, and the three-layer fix we shipped.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Google Translate breaks React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React keeps references to the DOM nodes it created, including plain text nodes. When state changes, it updates or removes those exact nodes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Google Translate doesn't know about React. When it translates a page, it walks the DOM and &lt;strong&gt;replaces text nodes&lt;/strong&gt; with its own &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;font&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; elements containing the translated text:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- What React rendered --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Save&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- What the DOM looks like after Google Translate --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;button&amp;gt;&amp;lt;font&amp;gt;&amp;lt;font&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;保存&lt;span class="nt"&gt;&amp;lt;/font&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/font&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The original &lt;code&gt;"Save"&lt;/code&gt; text node is gone from the DOM, but React still holds a reference to it. The next time React needs to remove or replace that text, it calls &lt;code&gt;parent.removeChild(textNode)&lt;/code&gt; — and the browser throws, because that node is no longer a child of anything.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same thing happens with &lt;code&gt;insertBefore&lt;/code&gt; when React tries to insert something next to a node that Translate has swapped out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's a long-standing issue — &lt;a href="https://github.com/facebook/react/issues/11538" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;facebook/react#11538&lt;/a&gt; has been open since 2017 — and it isn't specific to React: anything that holds references to text nodes is vulnerable. If you want the deep dive, &lt;a href="https://martijnhols.nl/gists/everything-about-google-translate-crashing-react" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Martijn Hols' write-up&lt;/a&gt; is excellent.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Which code is vulnerable
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The crash needs two things: a &lt;strong&gt;bare text node&lt;/strong&gt; and something &lt;strong&gt;conditional&lt;/strong&gt; next to it. Patterns like these:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Text sitting next to a conditional element&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSaving&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Spinner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  Save
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Conditional text&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Ternary returning strings&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSaving&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Saving…&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Saved&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Text mixed with an expression&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Uploaded &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; files&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every QR builder has dozens of these: status labels, counters, "Uploading… / Done", plan badges. Which is why the crash hit our most active user and nobody else.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Reproducing it without Google Translate
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Waiting for a translated session to show up in your logs is not a test plan. You can simulate what Translate does to the DOM in the browser console:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fakeTranslate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;walker&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createTreeWalker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NodeFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;SHOW_TEXT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="na"&gt;acceptNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodeValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;trim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parentElement&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parentElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;closest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;script, style, [translate="no"], font&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NodeFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;FILTER_ACCEPT&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;NodeFilter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;FILTER_REJECT&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[];&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;while &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;nextNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;())&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;walker&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currentNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;for &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;textNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;outer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;font&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;document&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createElement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;font&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;inner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;textContent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;译&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;textNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodeValue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// mark it as "translated"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;outer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;appendChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;inner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nx"&gt;textNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parentNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replaceChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;outer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;textNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;nodes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;CRASH:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;fakeTranslate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Paste it, run &lt;code&gt;fakeTranslate()&lt;/code&gt;, then use the app: switch tabs, toggle options, type into inputs, navigate between routes. Run &lt;code&gt;fakeTranslate()&lt;/code&gt; again after each step, because real Translate keeps re-translating new content as it appears.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On our dashboard, switching QR types after this reproduced the exact crash from the recording within a few clicks.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The fix: three layers
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There's no single clean fix. What worked for us is three layers, from "never crash" to "fewer weird states".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Layer 1: a DOM guard so the crash can't happen
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the workaround from the React issue thread: patch &lt;code&gt;removeChild&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;insertBefore&lt;/code&gt; so that, instead of throwing, they skip the operation when the node relationship is no longer what React expects.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// src/lib/domTranslateGuard.ts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;installDomTranslateGuard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;():&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Node&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;prototype&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;__translateGuardInstalled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;__translateGuardInstalled&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;originalRemoveChild&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;removeChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;removeChild&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;function &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parentNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;warn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;[dom-guard] removeChild skipped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clarity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dom_guard_removeChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;originalRemoveChild&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;child&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;originalInsertBefore&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;insertBefore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nx"&gt;proto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;insertBefore&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;function &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;newNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Node&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;referenceNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Node&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;referenceNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;referenceNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parentNode&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;warn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;[dom-guard] insertBefore skipped&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;referenceNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;as &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kr"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;clarity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;event&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dom_guard_insertBefore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;newNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;originalInsertBefore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;newNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;referenceNode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Two details that matter:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Install it before React touches the DOM.&lt;/strong&gt; We call it as the very first thing in the client entry, before &lt;code&gt;hydrateRoot&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// entry-client.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;installDomTranslateGuard&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;./lib/domTranslateGuard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;installDomTranslateGuard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ...then hydrateRoot(...)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep it out of SSR.&lt;/strong&gt; It only lives in the client entry, and the &lt;code&gt;typeof window&lt;/code&gt; check is a second line of defence. The server never touches &lt;code&gt;Node.prototype&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The trade-off is honest: this hides the error instead of fixing the cause. A skipped &lt;code&gt;insertBefore&lt;/code&gt; can occasionally leave a piece of UI missing until the next render. That's why we log it and send a custom event to our session analytics — so we can see how often the guard actually fires, and on which pages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Layer 2: stop giving Translate bare text nodes
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The guard prevents crashes. Wrapping text in elements prevents most of the situations where it would have to step in. If text lives inside its own &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, Translate replaces the text &lt;em&gt;inside&lt;/em&gt; the span, and React only ever adds or removes the span itself — which is still there.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSaving&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Spinner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  Save
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// After&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isSaving&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Spinner&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Save&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// After&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Before&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Uploaded &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; files&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// After&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Uploaded &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; files&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No visual change, no new classes. We went through every component in the QR builder, the file upload flow, the editor and the download modals, and wrapped anything that changes at runtime: status labels, counters, button text next to spinners.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Layer 3: &lt;code&gt;translate="no"&lt;/code&gt; — but only where it makes sense
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The tempting shortcut is &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html translate="no"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. Don't. Your users turned on translation because they need it — breaking the crash by breaking the translation just moves the problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We only opt out content that &lt;strong&gt;shouldn't&lt;/strong&gt; be translated anyway:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;URL, email, phone and password inputs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;short links and destination URLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the QR preview and technical labels (sizes, PNG/SVG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;the brand name in the header and footer
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"url"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;translate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"no"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;translate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"no"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;shortUrl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Everything else — headings, buttons, help text — still gets translated.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  How we verified it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After deploying, I ran the fake-translate script on the live site: the public PDF QR generator, then the logged-in dashboard. I switched QR types back and forth, toggled the logo option, typed into inputs, and navigated from the builder to the landing page editor and back — re-running &lt;code&gt;fakeTranslate()&lt;/code&gt; after each step.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Result: zero uncaught errors, no reloads, and the UI kept updating live with the "translated" text in place. The brand name and URL fields stayed untouched, as intended.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We'll keep watching the &lt;code&gt;dom_guard_*&lt;/code&gt; events in session analytics. If they show up a lot on a specific page, that page still has bare text nodes to wrap.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Google Translate replaces text nodes with &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;font&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; elements. React still holds the old nodes and crashes on &lt;code&gt;removeChild&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;insertBefore&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can reproduce it without Translate by wrapping text nodes in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;font&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; from the console.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Layer 1:&lt;/strong&gt; patch &lt;code&gt;removeChild&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;insertBefore&lt;/code&gt; before hydration, client-only, and log when it fires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Layer 2:&lt;/strong&gt; wrap conditional and dynamic text in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Layer 3:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;translate="no"&lt;/code&gt; only on inputs, URLs and brand names — never on the whole app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The part that stuck with me: this bug hit the single most engaged user we had that month. International users who translate your app are often exactly the people working hardest to use it.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;I'm building &lt;a href="https://qrflows.app" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;QRflows&lt;/a&gt; in public — dynamic QR codes with Smart Rules, real-time analytics and a Claude MCP integration. If you've hit this bug with a different framework, I'd like to hear how you handled it.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  TL;DR
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The right Sonner alternative depends on what Sonner does not do for you, and if nothing is wrong, keep it: it is by far the most downloaded of the four toast libraries compared here and has a stack, swipe and promise toasts built in. Pick react-hot-toast for the smallest bundle (4.8 kB gzip) and a headless hook, or React-Toastify for progress bars, a queue limit and a notification history. Pick a source-owned toast, such as the free Wingo UI Toast, when you need to change how the stack behaves on phones, for screen readers or in your design system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You go looking for a Sonner alternative when something about the toast stops fitting: the bundle, a design system that fights its stylesheet, an accessibility review, or action buttons that are hard to hit on a phone. Sonner is still the default React toast for good reasons, so leaving it should fix a specific problem. This comparison puts Sonner next to react-hot-toast, React-Toastify and a source-owned toast on the API, the stack, swipe, screen readers, phones and bundle size, checked in October 2026 against each package's published code and docs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We build Wingo UI, whose free Toast is the source-owned option here, so read this as a vendor's comparison with sources; it says where each of the others is the better pick. More head to head comparisons live under &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/category/comparisons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Comparisons and alternatives&lt;/a&gt;, and the &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/blog/shadcn-alternatives" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;guide to shadcn alternatives&lt;/a&gt; compares whole component libraries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What is the best Sonner alternative for React?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The best Sonner alternative depends on what you are leaving for:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;A smaller bundle and your own markup:&lt;/strong&gt; react-hot-toast. It measured 4.8 kB gzip in our build, half of Sonner, and its &lt;code&gt;useToaster&lt;/code&gt; hook lets you render every toast yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;More features built in:&lt;/strong&gt; React-Toastify. Progress bars, a queue &lt;code&gt;limit&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;toast.update&lt;/code&gt;, a stacked mode, RTL and a notification history add-on, with no extra packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Behavior you can change:&lt;/strong&gt; a toast whose source lives in your repository, such as the free Wingo UI &lt;a href="https://wingo-ui.com/components/toast" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Toast&lt;/a&gt;. It keeps a Sonner-style &lt;code&gt;toast()&lt;/code&gt; API, and the stack, the timers and the phone layout are code you can edit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No problem to fix:&lt;/strong&gt; stay on Sonner. It is the most downloaded React toast notification library of the four by a wide margin, and shadcn/ui installs it for Radix and React Aria projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

